/-!
# Finite type sheaves of modules are closed under extensions

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a topological space `T`. If
`0 ⟶ ℱ₁ ⟶ ℱ₂ ⟶ ℱ₃ ⟶ 0` is a short exact sequence of sheaves of `R`-modules and both `ℱ₁` and
`ℱ₃` are of finite type, then so is `ℱ₂`. This is the second assertion of Stacks Tag 01B7; the
first assertion, that the image of a morphism out of a sheaf of modules of finite type is of
finite type, is proved here as well.

The proof is the one in the Stacks Project: finite type is a local condition, and near a point
`x` one may choose an open `V` on which `ℱ₁` and `ℱ₃` are both generated by finitely many
sections. Since `ℱ₂ ⟶ ℱ₃` is an epimorphism its sections are locally in the image, so after
shrinking `V` to an open `W ∋ x` the finitely many generators of `ℱ₃` lift to sections of `ℱ₂`.
Those lifts together with the images of the generators of `ℱ₁` generate `ℱ₂` over `W`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalOver` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mkOver`: the bijection between the
  global sections of the restriction `M.over V` and the sections of `M` over `V`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeSumHom`: the morphism `free (A ⊕ B) ⟶ M` determined by a pair of
  morphisms `free A ⟶ M` and `free B ⟶ M`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfEpi`: the generating sections attached to an
  epimorphism out of a free sheaf of modules.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.restrictFreeHom`: restriction of a morphism out of a free sheaf of
  modules along a morphism `W ⟶ V` of the site.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataOfEpi` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataOfPointwise`: local generators data pushed forward
  along an epimorphism, and local generators data assembled from pointwise data on a space.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeAt`: a sheaf of modules on a space is of finite type at a
  point if some open neighbourhood of that point carries finitely many generating sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_iff_forall_isFiniteTypeAt`: on a topological space, being
  of finite type is the pointwise condition `IsFiniteTypeAt`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.epi_freeSumHom`: the categorical core. If `g` is a cokernel of `f`, if
  `free A ⟶ M₁` is an epimorphism and if `l : free B ⟶ M₂` is such that `l ≫ g` is an
  epimorphism, then `free (A ⊕ B) ⟶ M₂` built from these data is an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_lifts_of_epi`: finitely many sections of the target of an
  epimorphism lift simultaneously on a neighbourhood of any given point.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi`: a quotient of a sheaf of modules of finite type is
  of finite type, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_image`: **Stacks Tag 01B7**, first
  assertion, the image of a morphism out of a sheaf of modules of finite type is of finite type.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_middle_of_shortExact`: **Stacks Tag 01B7**, second
  assertion, the middle term of a short exact sequence of sheaves of modules with outer terms of
  finite type is of finite type.

## Implementation notes

The statement is proved for an arbitrary sheaf of rings on an arbitrary topological space, rather
than for the structure sheaf of a ringed space: nothing in the argument uses commutativity or the
specific sheaf of rings, only that the site is the site of opens of a space. The only place where
the topology of a space is used is the equivalence between finite type and the pointwise condition
`IsFiniteTypeAt`, which rests on the fact that for the topology of a space a covering sieve of `U`
contains, for each point of `U`, an arrow from an open neighbourhood of that point. Everything
else is proved over a general site.

Universes are forced rather than chosen. `Mathlib`'s `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` quantifies over
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData.{u'}` where `u'` is the universe of the objects of the site, so
for `T : Type u` the covering of the terminal object must be indexed in `Type u`. The covering used
to prove the pointwise criterion is indexed by the points of `T` itself, which is exactly what that
universe allows.

The restriction `M.over V` of a sheaf of modules along an open is `Mathlib`'s
`SheafOfModules.overFunctor`, a sheaf of modules on the slice site `Over V`. Its global sections
are a compatible family indexed by `Over V`, and `evalOver` reads off the component at the terminal
object `Over.mk (𝟙 V)`, which is the actual section over `V`; `mkOver` is the inverse, obtained by
restricting along the structure morphism of each slice object. The restriction functors
`overFunctor R V` and `overMap R f` are left adjoints, hence additive and colimit preserving; that
is what makes `restrictFreeHom` preserve epimorphisms and lets a cokernel of the original sequence
restrict to a cokernel of the restricted one. Those two instances are not found by
`infer_instance` on `overFunctor` in `Mathlib` because `overFunctor` is a `def` whose body is a
`pushforward`, so they are restated here.

The `IsFiniteType` instances are built with the explicit field name
`exists_localGeneratorsData := Exists.intro ..` rather than with anonymous constructor notation.
This is forced: the anonymous constructor of `IsFiniteType` does not propagate the expected type
into the existential it wraps, and defaults the universes of
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData` to `0`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace SheafOfModules

universe v u u'

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### Sections of a restriction -/

section Eval

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {V : C}

/-- The section over `V` underlying a global section of the restriction `M.over V`: the component
of the compatible family at the terminal object of `Over V`. -/
noncomputable def evalOver (s : (M.over V).sections) : M.val.presheaf.obj (op V) :=
  s.val (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))

/-- A section of `M` over `V`, read as a global section of the restriction `M.over V`: the
component at a slice object is the restriction along its structure morphism. -/
noncomputable def mkOver (t : M.val.presheaf.obj (op V)) : (M.over V).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun W => M.val.presheaf.map (W.unop.hom).op t) (by
    intro W W' φ
    change M.val.presheaf.map (φ.unop.left).op (M.val.presheaf.map (W.unop.hom).op t)
      = M.val.presheaf.map (W'.unop.hom).op t
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp, Over.w φ.unop])

/-- `evalOver` is a left inverse of `mkOver`. -/
@[simp]
lemma evalOver_mkOver (t : M.val.presheaf.obj (op V)) :
    evalOver (mkOver (M := M) (V := V) t) = t := by
  show M.val.presheaf.map (𝟙 V).op t = t
  rw [op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  rfl

/-- `mkOver` is a left inverse of `evalOver`. -/
lemma mkOver_evalOver (s : (M.over V).sections) : mkOver (evalOver s) = s := by
  apply PresheafOfModules.sections_ext
  rintro ⟨W⟩
  exact s.property (Over.homMk W.hom (Category.comp_id _) : W ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 V)).op

/-- A global section of `M.over V` is determined by its section over `V`. -/
lemma evalOver_injective : Function.Injective (evalOver (M := M) (V := V)) := fun s s' h => by
  rw [← mkOver_evalOver s, ← mkOver_evalOver s', h]

variable (M N) in
/-- The underlying morphism of presheaves of abelian groups of a morphism of sheaves of modules.
Sections and their restrictions are read off at this level: the restriction maps of a presheaf of
*modules* are semilinear, so their codomain carries a `ModuleCat.restrictScalars` wrapper which
blocks rewriting, whereas the underlying presheaf of abelian groups has none. -/
noncomputable abbrev toAb (h : M ⟶ N) : M.val.presheaf ⟶ N.val.presheaf :=
  (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map h.val

/-- `evalOver` is natural in the sheaf of modules. -/
lemma evalOver_sectionsMap (h : M ⟶ N) (s : (M.over V).sections) :
    evalOver (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap (h.over V) s) = (toAb M N h).app (op V) (evalOver s) :=
  rfl

end Eval

/-! ### Morphisms out of a free sheaf of modules -/

section Free

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {A B : Type u}

/-- The morphism out of `free (A ⊕ B)` whose restrictions along the two summand inclusions are
the given morphisms `p` and `q`. -/
noncomputable def freeSumHom (p : free A ⟶ M) (q : free B ⟶ M) : free (A ⊕ B) ⟶ M :=
  M.freeHomEquiv.symm (Sum.elim (M.freeHomEquiv p) (M.freeHomEquiv q))

/-- Restricting `freeSumHom p q` along the inclusion of the summand `A` gives `p`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma freeMap_inl_freeSumHom (p : free A ⟶ M) (q : free B ⟶ M) :
    freeMap Sum.inl ≫ freeSumHom p q = p :=
  M.freeHomEquiv.injective (funext fun a ↦ by
    rw [freeHomEquiv_comp_apply, freeHomEquiv_freeMap]
    exact sectionsMap_freeHomEquiv_symm_freeSection _ (Sum.inl a))

/-- Restricting `freeSumHom p q` along the inclusion of the summand `B` gives `q`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma freeMap_inr_freeSumHom (p : free A ⟶ M) (q : free B ⟶ M) :
    freeMap Sum.inr ≫ freeSumHom p q = q :=
  M.freeHomEquiv.injective (funext fun b ↦ by
    rw [freeHomEquiv_comp_apply, freeHomEquiv_freeMap]
    exact sectionsMap_freeHomEquiv_symm_freeSection _ (Sum.inr b))

/-- The generating sections of `M` attached to an epimorphism out of a free sheaf of modules. -/
@[simps I s]
noncomputable def generatingSectionsOfEpi {I : Type u} (p : free I ⟶ M) [Epi p] :
    M.GeneratingSections where
  I := I
  s := M.freeHomEquiv p
  epi := by
    rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
    infer_instance

/-- The generating sections attached to an epimorphism out of a free sheaf of modules on a finite
type are of finite type. -/
instance {I : Type u} (p : free I ⟶ M) [Epi p] [Finite I] :
    (generatingSectionsOfEpi p).IsFiniteType :=
  ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite I)⟩

end Free

/-! ### The categorical core -/

section Core

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- Let `g : M₂ ⟶ M₃` be a cokernel of `f : M₁ ⟶ M₂`, let `p : free A ⟶ M₁` be an epimorphism and
let `l : free B ⟶ M₂` be such that `l ≫ g` is an epimorphism. Then `M₂` is generated by the image
of `p` together with `l`, that is, `freeSumHom (p ≫ f) l : free (A ⊕ B) ⟶ M₂` is an epimorphism.
This is the categorical content of the second assertion of the extension result below: the sub is
generated by `A` sections, the quotient by `B` sections which lift to `M₂`, so the middle term is
generated by `A ⊕ B` sections. -/
theorem epi_freeSumHom {M₁ M₂ M₃ : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {f : M₁ ⟶ M₂} {g : M₂ ⟶ M₃}
    {hfg : f ≫ g = 0} (hg : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ g hfg))
    {A B : Type u} (p : free A ⟶ M₁) [Epi p] (l : free B ⟶ M₂) [Epi (l ≫ g)] :
    Epi (freeSumHom (p ≫ f) l) := by
  rw [Preadditive.epi_iff_cancel_zero]
  intro Z h hh
  have h1 : f ≫ h = 0 := (cancel_epi p).mp <| by
    simpa [hh] using (freeMap_inl_freeSumHom_assoc (p ≫ f) l h).symm
  have hgd : g ≫ hg.desc (CokernelCofork.ofπ h h1) = h := Cofork.IsColimit.π_desc hg
  have h2 : hg.desc (CokernelCofork.ofπ h h1) = 0 := (cancel_epi (l ≫ g)).mp <| by
    simpa [hgd, hh] using (freeMap_inr_freeSumHom_assoc (p ≫ f) l h).symm
  rw [← hgd, h2, comp_zero]

end Core

/-! ### Restriction along a morphism of the site -/

section Restrict

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v} C] [HasBinaryProducts C] [HasPullbacks C]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (X : C), HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (X : C), (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The restriction functor `overFunctor R W` is a left adjoint. This is `Mathlib`'s instance for
`SheafOfModules.pushforward (𝟙 (R.over W))`, which instance search does not see through the
definition of `overFunctor`. -/
noncomputable instance isLeftAdjoint_overFunctor (W : C) :
    (overFunctor.{u} R W).IsLeftAdjoint :=
  inferInstanceAs (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (𝟙 (R.over W))).IsLeftAdjoint

/-- The restriction functor `overFunctor R W` is additive, being a left adjoint between additive
categories. -/
noncomputable instance additive_overFunctor (W : C) : (overFunctor.{u} R W).Additive :=
  have : PreservesBinaryBiproducts (overFunctor.{u} R W) :=
    preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBinaryCoproducts _
  Functor.additive_of_preservesBinaryBiproducts _

variable {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {I : Type u} {V W : C}

/-- Restriction along `f : W ⟶ V` of a morphism out of a free sheaf of modules. -/
noncomputable def restrictFreeHom (f : W ⟶ V) (p : free I ⟶ M.over V) : free I ⟶ M.over W :=
  (mapFreeIso (overMap R f) I (overMapUnitIso (R := R) f).symm).hom ≫
    (overMap R f).map p ≫ ((overFunctorMap R f).app M).hom

/-- The restriction of an epimorphism out of a free sheaf of modules is an epimorphism. -/
instance epi_restrictFreeHom (f : W ⟶ V) (p : free I ⟶ M.over V) [Epi p] :
    Epi (restrictFreeHom f p) := by
  unfold restrictFreeHom
  infer_instance

omit [HasBinaryProducts C] [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The sections generating a restricted free presentation are the restrictions of the original
generating sections. -/
lemma evalOver_freeHomEquiv_restrictFreeHom (f : W ⟶ V) (p : free I ⟶ M.over V) (i : I) :
    evalOver ((M.over W).freeHomEquiv (restrictFreeHom f p) i)
      = M.val.presheaf.map f.op (evalOver ((M.over V).freeHomEquiv p i)) := by
  have key : ∀ (s : (M.over V).sections),
      s.val (op ((Over.map f).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 W))))
        = M.val.presheaf.map f.op (evalOver s) :=
    fun s => (s.property (Over.homMk f (by simp) :
      (Over.map f).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 W)) ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 V)).op).symm
  have h1 : (M.over W).freeHomEquiv (restrictFreeHom f p) i
      = (M.over W).unitHomEquiv ((overMapUnitIso (R := R) f).symm.hom ≫
        (overMap R f).map (ιFree i ≫ p) ≫ ((overFunctorMap R f).app M).hom) := by
    show (M.over W).unitHomEquiv (ιFree i ≫ restrictFreeHom f p) = _
    congr 1
    rw [restrictFreeHom, ← Category.assoc, ιFree_mapFreeIso_hom]
    simp [Functor.map_comp]
  rw [h1, ← key]
  rfl

/-- A cokernel of `f` restricts to a cokernel of the restriction of `f`, because the restriction
functor is additive and preserves colimits. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCokernelCoforkOver {M₁ M₂ M₃ : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {f : M₁ ⟶ M₂}
    {g : M₂ ⟶ M₃} {hfg : f ≫ g = 0} (hg : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ g hfg)) (W : C) :
    IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ (g.over W)
      (show (f.over W) ≫ (g.over W) = 0 by rw [← Functor.map_comp, hfg, Functor.map_zero])) :=
  CokernelCofork.mapIsColimit _ hg (overFunctor R W)

end Restrict

/-! ### Quotients and images -/

section Image

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v} C]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (X : C), HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (X : C), (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : C, PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (overFunctor.{u} R V)]
  {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R}

/-- Restriction to a slice site preserves epimorphisms, because it preserves colimits. The
hypothesis is the colimit preservation itself rather than binary products on the site, which is
only one way to get it. -/
noncomputable local instance preservesEpimorphisms_overFunctor (V : C) :
    (overFunctor.{u} R V).PreservesEpimorphisms := by
  have : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} (overFunctor.{u} R V) :=
    preservesColimitsOfSize_shrink _
  have : PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingSpan (overFunctor.{u} R V) := inferInstance
  infer_instance

/-- Local generators data pushed forward along an epimorphism: the covering is unchanged and each
generating family is replaced by the family of its images. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataOfEpi (σ : M.LocalGeneratorsData) (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] :
    N.LocalGeneratorsData where
  I := σ.I
  X := σ.X
  coversTop := σ.coversTop
  generators i := (σ.generators i).ofEpi (p.over (σ.X i))

/-- Local generators data of finite type push forward along an epimorphism to local generators
data of finite type. -/
instance isFiniteType_localGeneratorsDataOfEpi (σ : M.LocalGeneratorsData) (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    [h : σ.IsFiniteType] : (localGeneratorsDataOfEpi σ p).IsFiniteType where
  isFiniteType i :=
    have := h.isFiniteType i
    inferInstanceAs ((σ.generators i).ofEpi (p.over (σ.X i))).IsFiniteType

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- A quotient of a sheaf of modules of finite type is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_epi (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hM.exists_localGeneratorsData
  exact { exists_localGeneratorsData :=
    Exists.intro (localGeneratorsDataOfEpi σ p) inferInstance }

/-- The image of a morphism out of a sheaf of modules of finite type is of finite type. -/
@[stacks 01B7 "finite_type_image"]
theorem isFiniteType_image (φ : M ⟶ N) (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : (image φ).IsFiniteType :=
  isFiniteType_of_epi (factorThruImage φ) hM

end Image

/-! ### Finite type is a pointwise condition on a space -/

section Space

variable {T : Type u} [TopologicalSpace T]
  {R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology T) RingCat.{u}}

/-- A sheaf of modules on a topological space is **of finite type at a point** `x` if some open
neighbourhood of `x` carries finitely many generating sections. -/
def IsFiniteTypeAt (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (x : T) : Prop :=
  ∃ (V : Opens T) (_ : x ∈ V) (σ : (M.over V).GeneratingSections), σ.IsFiniteType

/-- A sheaf of modules of finite type is of finite type at every point. -/
lemma isFiniteTypeAt_of_isFiniteType (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (hM : M.IsFiniteType) (x : T) :
    IsFiniteTypeAt M x := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hM.exists_localGeneratorsData
  obtain ⟨U, _, ⟨i, ⟨j⟩⟩, hxU⟩ := σ.coversTop ⊤ x (by trivial)
  exact ⟨σ.X i, leOfHom j hxU, σ.generators i, hσ.isFiniteType i⟩

/-- Local generators data assembled from a pointwise choice of open neighbourhood together with
generating sections there. The covering of the terminal object is indexed by the points of the
space, which is why `IsFiniteType` can be checked pointwise. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataOfPointwise {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (V : T → Opens T)
    (hV : ∀ x, x ∈ V x) (σ : ∀ x, (M.over (V x)).GeneratingSections) :
    SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData M where
  I := T
  X := V
  coversTop Z y hyZ := ⟨V y ⊓ Z, homOfLE inf_le_right, ⟨y, ⟨homOfLE inf_le_left⟩⟩, hV y, hyZ⟩
  generators := σ

/-- A sheaf of modules on a topological space which is of finite type at every point is of finite
type. -/
lemma isFiniteType_of_forall_isFiniteTypeAt (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R)
    (h : ∀ x : T, IsFiniteTypeAt M x) : M.IsFiniteType := by
  choose V hxV σ hσ using h
  have hlgd : (localGeneratorsDataOfPointwise (M := M) V hxV σ).IsFiniteType := by
    constructor
    exact hσ
  -- the explicit field name is needed: the anonymous constructor of `IsFiniteType` does not
  -- propagate the expected type into the existential, and defaults its universes to `0`
  exact { exists_localGeneratorsData :=
    Exists.intro (localGeneratorsDataOfPointwise (M := M) V hxV σ) hlgd }

/-- On a topological space, a sheaf of modules is of finite type exactly when it is of finite type
at every point. -/
theorem isFiniteType_iff_forall_isFiniteTypeAt (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    M.IsFiniteType ↔ ∀ x : T, IsFiniteTypeAt M x :=
  ⟨fun hM => isFiniteTypeAt_of_isFiniteType M hM, isFiniteType_of_forall_isFiniteTypeAt M⟩

/-! ### Local lifting of sections through an epimorphism -/

variable {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R}

/-- A section of the target of an epimorphism of sheaves of modules lifts on a neighbourhood of
any point of its domain of definition. -/
lemma exists_lift_of_epi (g : M ⟶ N) [Epi g] {U : Opens T} (t : N.val.presheaf.obj (op U))
    (x : T) (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ (V : Opens T) (hVU : V ≤ U), x ∈ V ∧ ∃ w : M.val.presheaf.obj (op V),
      (toAb M N g).app (op V) w = N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op t := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hS'⟩ := EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi g t
  obtain ⟨V, j, hj, hxV⟩ := hS x hxU
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hS' j hj
  exact ⟨V, leOfHom j, hxV, w, hw⟩

/-- Persistence of a lift under further restriction. -/
private lemma lift_restrict (g : M ⟶ N) {U V W : Opens T} (hVU : V ≤ U) (hWV : W ≤ V)
    (hWU : W ≤ U) (t : N.val.presheaf.obj (op U)) (w : M.val.presheaf.obj (op V))
    (hw : (toAb M N g).app (op V) w = N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op t) :
    (toAb M N g).app (op W) (M.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op w)
      = N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op t := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, (toAb M N g).naturality (homOfLE hWV).op,
    ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hw, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp]
  rfl

/-- Finitely many sections of the target of an epimorphism of sheaves of modules lift
simultaneously on a neighbourhood of any point. -/
lemma exists_lifts_of_epi (g : M ⟶ N) [Epi g] {U : Opens T} {B : Type u} [Finite B]
    (t : B → N.val.presheaf.obj (op U)) (x : T) (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ (V : Opens T) (hVU : V ≤ U), x ∈ V ∧ ∃ w : B → M.val.presheaf.obj (op V),
      ∀ b, (toAb M N g).app (op V) (w b) = N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (t b) := by
  classical
  suffices H : ∀ (s : Finset B), ∃ (V : Opens T) (hVU : V ≤ U), x ∈ V ∧
      ∃ w : B → M.val.presheaf.obj (op V),
        ∀ b ∈ s, (toAb M N g).app (op V) (w b)
          = N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (t b) by
    have := Fintype.ofFinite B
    obtain ⟨V, hVU, hxV, w, hw⟩ := H Finset.univ
    exact ⟨V, hVU, hxV, w, fun b => hw b (Finset.mem_univ b)⟩
  intro s
  induction s using Finset.induction with
  | empty => exact ⟨U, le_refl U, hxU, fun _ => 0, by simp⟩
  | @insert a s _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨V, hVU, hxV, w, hw⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨V', hV'U, hxV', w', hw'⟩ := exists_lift_of_epi g (t a) x hxU
    refine ⟨V ⊓ V', le_trans inf_le_left hVU, ⟨hxV, hxV'⟩,
      Function.update
        (fun b => M.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : V ⊓ V' ≤ V)).op (w b)) a
        (M.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : V ⊓ V' ≤ V')).op w'), ?_⟩
    intro b hb
    by_cases hba : b = a
    · subst hba
      rw [Function.update_self]
      exact lift_restrict g hV'U (inf_le_right : V ⊓ V' ≤ V')
        (le_trans inf_le_left hVU) (t b) w' hw'
    · rw [Function.update_of_ne hba]
      exact lift_restrict g hVU (inf_le_left : V ⊓ V' ≤ V) (le_trans inf_le_left hVU) (t b) (w b)
        (hw b ((Finset.mem_insert.mp hb).resolve_left hba))

/-! ### Stacks Tag 01B7 -/

/-- Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a topological space. In a short exact sequence of sheaves of
`R`-modules, if the first and third terms are of finite type then so is the middle term. -/
@[stacks 01B7 "finite_type_extension", sga "6 I 3.3" "c) finite type"]
theorem isFiniteType_middle_of_shortExact (S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R))
    (hS : S.ShortExact) (h₁ : S.X₁.IsFiniteType) (h₃ : S.X₃.IsFiniteType) :
    S.X₂.IsFiniteType := by
  have hg : Epi S.g := hS.epi_g
  refine isFiniteType_of_forall_isFiniteTypeAt _ fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨V₁, hxV₁, σ₁, hσ₁⟩ := isFiniteTypeAt_of_isFiniteType _ h₁ x
  obtain ⟨V₃, hxV₃, σ₃, hσ₃⟩ := isFiniteTypeAt_of_isFiniteType _ h₃ x
  have hf₁ : Finite σ₁.I := hσ₁.finite
  have hf₃ : Finite σ₃.I := hσ₃.finite
  set V : Opens T := V₁ ⊓ V₃
  have hxV : x ∈ V := ⟨hxV₁, hxV₃⟩
  set q : free σ₃.I ⟶ S.X₃.over V :=
    restrictFreeHom (M := S.X₃) (homOfLE (inf_le_right : V ≤ V₃)) σ₃.π
  obtain ⟨W, hWV, hxW, w, hw⟩ := exists_lifts_of_epi S.g
    (fun b => evalOver ((S.X₃.over V).freeHomEquiv q b)) x hxV
  set p : free σ₁.I ⟶ S.X₁.over W :=
    restrictFreeHom (M := S.X₁) (homOfLE (le_trans hWV inf_le_left : W ≤ V₁)) σ₁.π
  set l : free σ₃.I ⟶ S.X₂.over W :=
    (S.X₂.over W).freeHomEquiv.symm (fun b => mkOver (w b)) with hl
  have hlq : l ≫ (S.g.over W) = restrictFreeHom (M := S.X₃) (homOfLE hWV) q := by
    refine (S.X₃.over W).freeHomEquiv.injective (funext fun b => evalOver_injective ?_)
    rw [freeHomEquiv_comp_apply, hl, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, evalOver_sectionsMap,
      evalOver_mkOver]
    exact (hw b).trans
      (evalOver_freeHomEquiv_restrictFreeHom (M := S.X₃) (homOfLE hWV) q b).symm
  have hepi : Epi (l ≫ (S.g.over W)) := by
    rw [hlq]
    infer_instance
  have : Epi (freeSumHom (p ≫ (S.f.over W)) l) :=
    epi_freeSumHom (isColimitCokernelCoforkOver hS.gIsCokernel W) p l
  exact ⟨W, hxW, generatingSectionsOfEpi (freeSumHom (p ≫ (S.f.over W)) l),
    ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite (σ₁.I ⊕ σ₃.I))⟩⟩

end Space

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

